[09/01/2025 07:54:30.689 PM] Message  || User: kitadan             || Channel: #yapper-committee                    || Content: Back before South Arlington got developed, it was a ranch.  The particular ranch was a peacock ranch.  The owner of the ranch went into debt and ran away rather than pay the bill.  So the peacocks became free range and went places other than the ranch.  When houses started being built in the area, the birds would come and go as they used to.  Eventually the owners of the houses just started feeding them.  They live and eat bugs in peoples yards.  That part of Arlington also has a large green space.
